+Tasks come in pages: the answer is `{ "items": [<task>, …], "next_cursor": "<opaque string>" | null }`, with the
+tasks in the order of the sort. Two more parameters:
+
+- `?limit=`: the size of a page, 1 to 200 (default 50); anything else answers 400;
+- `?cursor=`: the `next_cursor` of the previous page, passed back with the same filters and sort, answers the next
+  page. `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. A cursor only works with the list and the sort it came from: any
+  other value answers 400.
+
+A cursor marks a place in the order, not a copy of the list: tasks added, changed or deleted between two pages
+show up (or not) according to where they now sort. The page of the app
+shows the first page and has a "Load more" button for the next ones.
+
